pi-latex.js bundles renderLatex() from @earendil-works/pi-tui 1.0.1
(dist/latex.js and its width helpers), with get-east-asian-width.

- pi-tui: https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/tree/main/packages/tui
- get-east-asian-width: https://github.com/sindresorhus/get-east-asian-width

Both are MIT licensed. Their license texts follow the rebuild steps.

Rebuild after a Pi upgrade:

  P=/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent
  echo "export { renderLatex } from \"$P/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-tui/dist/latex.js\";" > /tmp/entry.js
  $P/node_modules/.bin/esbuild /tmp/entry.js --bundle --format=esm \
    --platform=neutral --minify-whitespace --outfile=hooks/vendor/pi-latex.js

